<title>UK: UK's Labour Party chalk up 10.2 percent swing.</title>
<headline>UK's Labour Party chalk up 10.2 percent swing.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a breakdown of the number of parliamentary seats each party has won in Britain's election, the share of votes each has polled, and the estimated final tally of seats for each party, with 658 results in from Britain's 659 constituencies -</p>
<p>    CONSERVATIVES.......165 (165 held, 177 lost)</p>
<p>    LABOUR..............419 (273 held, 146 gained)</p>
<p>LIBERAL DEMOCRATS....45 (18 held, 29 gained, 2 lost)</p>
<p>    OTHERS...............29 (19 held, 6 gained, 4 lost)</p>
<p>Average swing to Labour from Conservatives - 10.2 percent</p>
<p>Projected final total of seats according to BBC estimate -</p>
<p>    CONSERVATIVES.......165</p>
<p>    LABOUR..............419</p>
<p>LIBERAL DEMOCRATS....46</p>
<p>    OTHERS...............29</p>
<p>Predicted majority for Labour - 179</p>
<p>Share of the vote so far - Conservatives 31 percent, Labour 45 percent, Liberal Democrats 17 percent</p>
</text>
